10. migration / rollback needs: None; no service/data change. Amend through reviewed PR, preserve existing approved contracts/profiles and operational holds.
11. responsive / accessibility rules: N/A; no UI change. Owner summary uses plain-language outcomes.
12. evidence + handoff format: E-DEV-018 records normalized document digest, ten path classes, actual E10/CI, exact reviewed head/model/verdict, findings/closure and owner acceptance; unchanged runtime tests are regression evidence only.
13. graph-update records: T-E3-014/E-DEV-018 and registry/routing indexes; preserve T-E3-001-R1 REVIEW and physical HELD; no completion of follow-up tasks.
14. escalation rules: Missing authority/evidence holds capability. Provisioning/paid/privileged activation requires separately scoped work and owner-readable risk/cost/reversibility decisions; technical diagnosis stays with implementer.

